  "id": "Compound::DB01045 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Rifampicin appears to interact with Cyp2c9 through a shared pathway involving arachidonic acid metabolism. The evidence suggests that Rifampicin binds to Cyp2b6, which participates in both arachidonic acid monooxygenase and epoxygenase activities. These activities are ultimately linked to Cyp2c9, indicating a potential mechanism where Rifampicin influences Cyp2c9 through the modulation of arachidonic acid metabolism. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains partially inferred. The overlapping roles of Cyp2b6 in different arachidonic acid-related pathways highlight the possibility of Rifampicin acting as a modulator of Cyp2c9 via these intermediaries.",
